## 🎓 Key Learnings (For Future You)

### 1. Foundation First Pays Off
We spent time building Theme/i18n/utilities BEFORE features. Now:
- Features will be EASY to add (just use Theme & t())
- No refactoring debt
- High EROI (Energy Return on Interaction)

### 2. Single Source of Truth Works
- Colors? → `Theme.ts` (one place)
- Text? → `i18n/*.json` (one place per language)
- Types? → `types/*.ts` (one place)

**Benefit**: Change once, update everywhere!

### 3. Documentation is Code
DEVELOPER_REFERENCE.md will save you hours when you forget how things work.

### 4. Package Management Strategy
**Current rule**: Don't update packages until v0.1 is deployed.
**Why**: Stability > Latest features during foundation phase.
See [DEVELOPER_REFERENCE.md](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/DEVELOPER_REFERENCE.md) for update strategy.

